1. The finding and its rule

  ADV-R-8 [Major] of `measure/runs/model_guide/adversarial-deb8a21.json`.
  Two runs at the same time with the same route, set, and date computed the
  same pass number, shared one output folder, and clobbered one
  `.incoming-<diff>` file.

  The orchestrator and the PM chose option A on 2026-11-18. The runner takes
  one exclusive lock for one route, one set, and one date. It takes the lock
  before the pass number and before any call. A second run that finds the
  lock held exits 2 with one stderr line that names the lock, makes no call,
  and writes no pass record. The trap releases the lock on every exit path.

  The first Green attempt stopped, because the former ADV-R-8 required both
  runs to exit 0 with pass numbers 1 and 2. The Red rewrite 1b38ad8 makes
  ADV-R-8 follow option A. Green edited no test file.

2. Change

  `harness/model-guide/review-run.sh` holds the lock in
  `<private>/.locks/review-<set>-<route-slug>-<date>.lock` through `flock -n`
  on the file descriptor 9. The lock sits after the route, set, and diff
  checks, and before the pass number and the quota read. The `EXIT`, `INT`,
  and `TERM` traps reach `on_exit`, which runs `flock -u 9` and closes the
  descriptor. The lock refusal prints one line on stderr and writes no pass
  record. The script header names the new rule.

  No other file changed. `harness/opencode-credential.sh` and
  `harness/opencode-host.sh` did not change.

